      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخازر</span></b>  <i>He looked from the outer angle of
his eye.</i> (TA. [See also Q. Q. 1.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He pretended,</i> or <i>made a show of, what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَزَرٌ</span>:
[see 1.] (TA, and Har p. 62.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>He contracted
his eyelids, to sharpen the sight:</i> (S, Msb, K:)
a verb similar to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تعامى</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تجاهل</span>. (S. [See
also 2.])

